Demo scenes for the emulated GPU: host-written pushbuffers that drive the 3D (0xC797) and compute (0xC7C0) classes. GLSL in shaders/, register programs and memory maps in scenes/.
pbr-boombox: BoomBox or Avocado with metallic-roughness PBR and normal maps. Needs indexed u32 draws, depth, five mipmapped block-linear sampled textures.
post-effect: the PBR scene rendered offscreen, then a full-screen chromatic aberration, scanline and vignette pass. Needs render to texture by VA and vertex-less draws.
particles: 8192 particles integrated by a compute dispatch, drawn as additive instanced quads from the same buffer. Needs the compute class QMD launch, a compute-to-vertex barrier, per-instance streams, blending.
pbr-flighthelmet: FlightHelmet (95k triangles, six materials, 21 MB of textures) through the same PBR shaders, one draw per material, timed against pbr-boombox. Needs BEGIN-framed indexed draws and per-draw cbuf rebinds; run demos/assets/fetch.sh first.
raytraced: BoomBox on a ground plane with ray-query shadows and reflections in rt.frag plus ray-traced AO in rt_ao.comp. Needs acceleration structures (host-built), a compute pass after the draws, depth in guest memory.
sprites2d: parallax hill layers and floating sprites as alpha-blended instanced quads over a procedural atlas. Needs per-instance streams, alpha blending, repeat-wrap sampling.
Shaders compile with glslangValidator -V; the rig compiles them with the NVIDIA driver into the SM86 programs the scenes load. Values tagged (verify) in scenes/ are unconfirmed conventions.
Assets (demos/assets): BoomBox, Avocado and FlightHelmet by Microsoft, from KhronosGroup glTF-Sample-Assets, CC0 1.0 Universal; source URLs in each manifest.json. FlightHelmet is too big for the code branches, fetch.sh pulls it from the assets branch.
The sprites2d atlas is generated by the host at init, no asset file.
Shared setup (pushbuffer encoding, subchannels, SPH layout, cbuf slots, texture handles) is described once in scenes/pbr-boombox.md.
Every scene targets 1280x720 A8B8G8R8 pitch-linear, read back into display::present.
